From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 14:15:22 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 047/105] w8a16_gemv: optional two-destination column split in
 the epilogue

`w8a16_gemv` / `bf16_gemv` gain `out2=` + `split_n=`: the [M, N] result is
written to two caller-owned row-contiguous buffers, columns [0, split_n) to
`out` and [split_n, N) to `out2`. Only the store epilogue changes -- the k
loop, the fp32 accumulation order, the per-channel scale index and the bf16
rounding are untouched -- so the two buffers hold exactly the bytes a single
[M, N] output would have held. `SPLIT_N` is a constexpr defaulting to 0, so
every existing call compiles the original single-store epilogue.

This is the mechanism the GDN projection needs to produce mixed_qkv/z and b/a
directly, without the per-layer re-layout copy kernel.

Bit-exactness checked on GPU against the single-destination result for
(N=16384, split 10240) and (N=96, split 48) at M=1/4/16, plus an unaligned
split (37 of 96) that straddles a BLOCK_N tile: torch.equal on both halves.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
